ARM64EC: Restore page protections after patching dispatch slots.

NtProtectVirtualMemory requires a non-null old-protection output. Passing
nullptr when restoring FEX's dispatch-slot page returns ACCESS_VIOLATION
and leaves the originally read-only page writable. Supply the existing
local output variable, which is no longer needed after the restore.

Independent M4 probe checks the three CHPE dispatch slots against their
PE section write flags: before 0 pass / 3 fail (PAGE_WRITECOPY); after
3 / 0 (PAGE_READONLY). Memory 51/0, context 546/0, fibers 86/0 and
invalid-instruction context 108/0 remain unchanged. The probe is in
tests/fex-runtime; this is not evidence of FH6 gameplay.

--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
@@ -317,7 +317,7 @@
   ULONG Prot;
   NtProtectVirtualMemoryNative(NtCurrentProcess(), &ProtAddress, &ProtSize, PAGE_READWRITE, &Prot);
   *reinterpret_cast<T*>(Address) = Data;
-  NtProtectVirtualMemoryNative(NtCurrentProcess(), &ProtAddress, &ProtSize, Prot, nullptr);
+  NtProtectVirtualMemoryNative(NtCurrentProcess(), &ProtAddress, &ProtSize, Prot, &Prot);
 }
 
 void PatchCallChecker() {
